{"title":"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 89","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_89&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two perpendicular planes intersect a sphere in two circles. These circles intersect in two points, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/9/449d0044d36d91d32d21384b98fcb2bfce33ad12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />. If the radii of the two circles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1cb5bdce2d06d2419066a2b55ab01d824217bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$54$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d40f3652c1962e98ce050a88c04ed37997c67df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/6/62623d70eaa11458b42450ab31277cc88f4dbd6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R^2$\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the radius of the sphere.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_89&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of the sphere, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of the circle radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1cb5bdce2d06d2419066a2b55ab01d824217bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$54$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of the circle radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d40f3652c1962e98ce050a88c04ed37997c67df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/2/2a2f6cc057ed08d9fe871495515a8460d755954e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XM \\perp AB$\" width=\"88\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f1918e719d703e5391eb341234b73b656a656a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YM \\perp AB$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" />, by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/deb437482e8e5c76e39ecab26c376c2e60c6295f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XM = \\sqrt{54^2 - 21^2} = 15\\sqrt{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"225\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/d/d8d56dd538abdcf6a3fade25cef439b8892ac095.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YM = \\sqrt{66^2 - 21^2} = 3\\sqrt{435}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"223\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nAdditionally, by symmetry, the plane containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd85f7293ccb6c223872b3f78f8c105518115fe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X, M, Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> must also contain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Since the two planes are perpendicular, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d89db75f375671ce4e935088d7b554c9316725f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XM \\perp YM$\" width=\"94\" height=\"12\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b76221e8a81c70368a416be5681ab3635dc626be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OX \\perp XM$\" width=\"90\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/6/136a58ce42f731911a12e4e3d05058bf858420eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OY \\perp YM$\" width=\"87\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87b8e7f4801492b9c324ebed7c0989e9bee19198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OXMY$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> is a rectangle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/8/3d8061d4d2900d4fd82ccfe02ed955f80101c2a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OX = 3\\sqrt{435}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/2/f7259aadb63310f6e4009dc90b76046240c7cae0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(circle((0,0),100)); draw((-100,0)--(10,99.499)); draw((95,-31.225)--(-20,97.980));  dot((0,0)); label(&quot;O&quot;,(0,0),S);  pair X=(-45,49.750),Y=(37.5,33.376); draw(X--(0,0)--Y);  dot(X); label(&quot;X&quot;,X,NW); dot(Y); label(&quot;Y&quot;,Y,NE);  draw((0,0)--(-100,0),dotted); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Thus, by the Pythagorean Theorem the radius of the circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/2438a3628be9a0b89ff444be2a4de42ff34141e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{54^2 + 3915} = \\sqrt{6831}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cdfd8fcb5a56b37c6b2f3265a68ce15e96549aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R^2 = \\boxed{6831}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_89&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest\" title=\"2008 iTest\">2008 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_88\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 88\">Problem 88</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_90\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 90\">Problem 90</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Pr